      "message": "[From Jetski review] `BlockNode::Execute` does not run `CheckForUnusedVars` on scopes returned as values (`RETURNS_SCOPE`), and `dotfile_scope_.CheckForUnusedVars` does not recurse into nested scopes.\n\nBecause `included` is optional, a typo in `.gn` such as `{ includer \u003d \"//foo/*\", include \u003d \"//bar:baz\" }` will silently ignore `include` and grant a **global** exception to `//foo/*`.\n\nConsider checking for unknown keys in `scope` (e.g. via `scope-\u003eGetCurrentScopeValues()`, or by marking `\"includer\"` / `\"included\"` as used and calling `scope-\u003eCheckForUnusedVars(\u0026err)`).",
