      "message": "[From Jetski review] When `strict_exempt` is `true` but the include still fails because an intermediate dependency is private (e.g. `A -\u003e B --[private]--\u003e C` where `B` has `check_includes_strict \u003d true`), `GetDependencyChainPublicError(chain)` (lines 102-118) will still blame `B`\u0027s `check_includes_strict \u003d true` (\"Including headers from the public_deps of B is blocked because check_includes_strict \u003d true is enabled on it\") even though `strict_exempt` was already applied and the actual failure is the private dep.\n\nConsider passing `strict_exempt` (or checking `chain[i - 1].is_public` in `GetDependencyChainPublicError`) so the diagnostic does not blame `check_includes_strict` when it was exempted or when the link was actually private.",
